message: "If you use or discuss this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Behavioral Compilation: From Harness to Weights on a Single Machine"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Dagher
    given-names: Philippe
    email: philippe.dagher@senoni.com
    affiliation: "SENONI Research"
date-released: 2026-09-13
version: 1.0.0
abstract: >
  Production AI systems often accumulate domain expertise in discrete
  artifacts surrounding a frontier model. This paper asks whether the
  methodological structure of compiling stable organizational behavior
  into weights, while keeping mutable authority external, can be studied
  on a single local workstation. A rank-16 QLoRA adapter trained on five
  approved long-context review examples improved from 22/25 to 25/25
  labels and from 3/5 to 5/5 dispositions under a matched structured
  decoder. A later model-advisory found remaining evidence and authority
  defects. The result is exact-example decision fitting, not
  generalization or deployment readiness.
keywords:
